{
  "comment": "The agent configuration file the platform writes for a hosted agent and names in $GENFLEET_AGENT_CONFIG, shared byte-for-byte with the platform. version: an integer >= 1; a later version keeps these keys and may add more, which readers ignore. settings: {key: value}, only what the workspace saved, typed as the manifest declares. defaults: {key: value}, the manifest's defaults. A reader's value for a key is the saved one, else the default. connectors: {slot: {connection, provider, config, tools}} for the filled slots only. connections: {connection name: {provider, slot, tools}}, every connection the agent may use, in a slot or not (slot null). channels: {channel: {tools}}, each channel the agent has a live connection on. tools: [{name, tool, description, input_schema, definition_hash}], verified tools only; name is model-facing (<connection>__<tool>, or the bare name of a channel's built-in tool), [A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}, used as listed; input_schema is an object schema (type: object); definition_hash is 64 lowercase hex. A file without connections, channels or tools (an older platform) has no connector tools. A tool entry that is malformed is skipped, never renamed, and so is a malformed connections or channels entry (or either key when it is not an object); the rest of the file still reads. prompts: [{title, body}], the enabled ones in order. handoffs: {key: {kind, wired, options}}, one per hand-off the agent's manifest sends; wired is whether the workspace chose a destination; options holds every option with a value (saved, else the manifest's default). A file without handoffs (an older platform) has none, and a malformed entry is skipped. Each case: the file (an object, or raw text) and what a reader gets, or error: true. connector_tools: the model-facing names connector_tools() returns; slot_tools: per slot; reply: whether reply_tool() is offered. handoffs: what handoffs() returns (absent = none).",
